        "payment-runbook.md",
        "payment-service.md",
        "service-discovery.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Connectivity-oriented gRPC status codes, such as `UNAVAILABLE`, combined with the absence of a server span, suggest the failure occurred before the request arrived at PaymentService.",
      "sources": [
        "payment-service.md",
        "grpc-troubleshooting.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If a Payment server span exists, the failure occurred inside PaymentService, and investigators should inspect Payment application logs, gRPC server status, charge-processing errors, and downstream calls to identify business logic issues.",
